Q: How do I include an image from resources in my TWebBrowser page in Delphi? A: <p><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/previous-versions/windows/internet-explorer/ie-developer/platform-apis/jj710218(v=vs.85)" rel="nofollow noreferrer">This page</a> explains the `res` protocol, and shows the following example:</p>
<pre><code>&quot;res://mydll.dll/#2/#234&quot;
</code></pre>
<p>where <code>#234</code> is the string or numerical identifier of the resource. <code>#2</code> is the resource type. <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/menurc/resource-types" rel="nofollow noreferrer">This page</a> lists the defined resource types, and we see that <code>#2</code> corresponds to RT_BITMAP. Didn't work, but changing <code>#2</code> to <code>#10</code> (for RT_RCDATA) solved it. So the following HTML code does the job:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;img src=&quot;res://Circles.exe/#10/rc_geraldine&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: How do I make my Node.js server work with SINOTRACK ST-901 GPS tracker? A: <p>The device does not send text fields; it sends raw bytes.<br />
Therefore, the incoming TCP data must be handled as a <code>Buffer</code>, not strings, and parsed using byte offsets and bit masks.</p>
<pre><code>const buf = Buffer.from(chunk);
buf.readInt32BE(offset);
buf[offset];
bit masking ( &amp;, &gt;&gt; )
</code></pre>
